              "text": "The next NBA game is **Game 3 of the 2026 NBA Finals** between the **San Antonio Spurs** and the **New York Knicks**. The game will be played on **Monday, June 8, 2026, at 8:30 PM ET**, at **Madison Square Garden** in New York City.\n\nBecause the Knicks are in the Finals for the first time since 1999 and currently lead the series 2\u20130, ticket demand is at a historic, record-breaking high. \n\nSeveral reliable options are available to buy tickets, though prices are exceptionally steep.\n\n### 1. Official Primary Market (Face Value)\n* **Ticketmaster:** As the official ticketing partner of the NBA and the New York Knicks, Ticketmaster is the safest place to look for primary tickets and official verified resale tickets. \n\n### 2. Secondary/Resale Ticket Marketplaces\nBecause primary tickets sold out almost instantly, secondary marketplaces are your best bet for finding available seats. The most secure platforms with buyer protection guarantees include:\n* **SeatGeek:** The official fan-to-fan marketplace partner of many NBA teams.\n* **StubHub:** One of the largest resale platforms.\n* **TickPick:** Highly popular for buyers because they use \"all-in\" pricing, meaning there are no hidden service fees added at checkout.\n* **Vivid Seats:** Another major and trusted ticket resale broker.\n\n### A Heads-up on Current Prices & Policies\n* **Extreme Pricing:** Due to unprecedented demand, the \"get-in\" price (the cheapest seats in the nosebleed sections) for Game 3 at Madison Square Garden is currently averaging **between $9,800 and $10,800 per ticket**. Lower-level and courtside seats are climbing into tens of thousands of dollars. \n* **Mobile-Only Entry:** Madison Square Garden is a strictly digital venue. Tickets must be displayed on your mobile device (via the Ticketmaster or MSG venues app). PDF printouts or screenshots of tickets will not be accepted at the gate.",
